            <fr:title text="Equalizer">Equalizer</fr:title>
            <fr:taxon>Definition</fr:taxon>
          </fr:frontmatter>
          <fr:mainmatter>
            <html:p>
  Let <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[c]]></fr:tex> and <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[d]]></fr:tex> be objects in a category <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\mathcal {C}]]></fr:tex> with two parallel morphisms <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[f , g : c \to  d]]></fr:tex>. The <html:em>equalizer</html:em> of <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[f]]></fr:tex> and <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[g]]></fr:tex>, if it exists, is the universal object <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\mathsf {eq}]]></fr:tex> with the following property:
  <html:ul><html:li>There is a morphism <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\pi  : \mathsf {eq} \to  c]]></fr:tex></html:li>
    <html:li><fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\pi  \circ  f = \pi  \circ  g]]></fr:tex></html:li></html:ul></html:p>
          </fr:mainmatter>
